<law>
	<structure>
		<unit label="title" identifier="38.2" level="1">Insurance</unit>
		<unit label="chapter" identifier="33" level="2">Life Insurance Policies</unit>
		<unit label="article" identifier="3" level="3">Industrial Life Insurance Policies</unit>
	</structure>
	<section_number>38.2-3351</section_number>
	<catch_line>Title</catch_line>
	<text>
		Each industrial life insurance policy shall have a title on its face that briefly and accurately describes the nature and form of the policy.
	</text>
	<history>Code 1950, § 38-434(10); 1952, c. 317, § 38.1-419; 1986, c. 562.</history>
</law>
